<ans># Niva Bupa Health Insurance Ltd — FY23 (Full Year Ended 31 March 2023) Financial Data

Below is the extracted financial data based on direct review of Niva Bupa's statutory FY23 Annual Report, the Regulation 52 (IRDAI public disclosure) financial statements, and the MGT-7 annual return.

## Key Notes on Methodology

- **Basis clarification**: Niva Bupa reports under **Indian GAAP (IGAAP)** only, as is standard for Indian general/health insurers. There is no IFRS-basis PAT or claims ratio published — these fields have been left blank rather than estimated.
- **NWP vs NEP**: The Regulation 52 disclosure explicitly labels the "Net Premium" figure as **Net Earned Premium (NEP)**, matching the annual report's P&L exactly. **Net Written Premium (NWP) is not separately disclosed** in any of the four source documents, so that value is left blank per the strict sourcing rule (rather than approximating it from the Net Retention Ratio).
- **Expense of Management (EoM) ratio**: The regulatory filing discloses this on **two bases** — 41% (to Gross Direct Premium Income, the statutory basis used for IRDAI's EoM Regulations compliance) and 53% (to Net Written Premium). The GDPI-based 41% is used as the primary "EoM ratio" figure since that is the basis on which the regulatory allowable-limit test is applied.
- **Combined ratio / generic Expense ratio**: These require a single, clearly labeled figure on a consistent premium base. Since the source documents mix NEP-based (claims ratio) and NWP/GDPI-based (commission, EoM) denominators without an explicitly published combined figure, both have been left **blank** rather than computed via a mixed-basis estimate.
- **Retail health GWP / market share**: The company-specific retail health premium split and market share are not separately broken out in these four documents (only industry-wide figures appear in market-context sections), so both are left blank.
- **Investment yield**: Not explicitly labeled/published as a standalone ratio in the sources reviewed; left blank rather than back-calculated from investment income/AUM to avoid introducing an estimate.
- **Net worth**: The statutory net worth of **₹831.12 crore** shown in the Reg. 52 five-year ratio table is the correct regulatory figure (distinct from gross paid-up capital + reserves on the balance sheet, which includes accumulated losses carried as a debit balance in the P&L account, not netted into "Reserves & Surplus").

